    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d732">

                <pb facs="0727" n="1461" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1461"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mavroyeni Bey to Mr. Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Turkish Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-01-16"><hi rendition="#italic">January 16,
                        1896</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>: His Excellency Tevfik
                    Pasha has just informed me that the Sublime Porte regrets that it can not comply
                    with Mr. Terrell’s request for permission for the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bancroft</hi> to pass through the strait, that vessel having been
                    authorized to remain at the disposal of the United States legation at
                    Constantinople.</p>
                <p>Your excellency knows perfectly well the earnest and sincere desire of the
                    Imperial Government to do all in its power to strengthen if possible the ties of
                    friendship which unite the two countries, but in this case a certain fact is
                    involved, to wit, that only the signatory Powers of the treaty of Paris enjoy
                    the right to have vessels of war permanently at Constantinople at the orders of
                    their respective embassies. Now, the United States Government does not appear in
                    the number of the signatories of that treaty. I am, consequently, sure that your
                    excellency will be pleased to take the foregoing into consideration.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mavroyeni.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
